# Unity Runtime Patterns

> For naming conventions and project structure, see `file-standards.mdc`

## MonoBehaviour Setup

```csharp
using Sirenix.OdinInspector;
using DG.Tweening;

[Title("Component Name")]
[SerializeField] private GameObject targetPrefab;

private void Awake()
{
    // Cache GetComponent calls here
}

private void Start()
{
    // Cache manager references here (see code-patterns.mdc)
}

private void OnDestroy()
{
    // CRITICAL: Kill tweens to prevent null reference errors
    DOTween.Kill(transform);
    DOTween.Kill(this);
}
```

## Event Subscription Lifecycle (Critical)

**Always pair OnEnable/OnDisable** - This pattern prevented stage progression bugs:

```csharp
private void OnEnable()
{
    GameEvents.OnWaveComplete += HandleWaveComplete;
    StageManager.OnStageLoaded += HandleStageLoaded;
}

private void OnDisable()
{
    GameEvents.OnWaveComplete -= HandleWaveComplete;
    StageManager.OnStageLoaded -= HandleStageLoaded;
}
```

**Why**: Objects can be enabled/disabled during gameplay. Start/OnDestroy miss re-enable scenarios.

## DOTween Patterns (Preferred for Animations)

### Basic Tweens
```csharp
using DG.Tweening;

// Transform tweens
transform.DOMove(targetPos, duration).SetEase(Ease.OutQuad);
transform.DOScale(1.2f, 0.3f).SetLoops(2, LoopType.Yoyo);
transform.DORotate(new Vector3(0, 360, 0), 1f, RotateMode.FastBeyond360);

// UI tweens
canvasGroup.DOFade(1f, fadeInDuration);
rectTransform.DOAnchorPos(targetPos, duration);

// Material/Color tweens
renderer.material.DOColor(Color.red, 0.5f);
image.DOColor(targetColor, duration);
```

### Sequences (Replace Nested Coroutines)
```csharp
// PREFERRED: DOTween sequence
private void ShowIntroSequence()
{
    DOTween.Sequence()
        .Append(canvasGroup.DOFade(1f, fadeInDuration))
        .AppendInterval(displayDuration)
        .Append(canvasGroup.DOFade(0f, fadeOutDuration))
        .OnComplete(() => panel.SetActive(false));
}

// AVOID: Nested coroutines for animations
// private IEnumerator ShowIntroSequence() { ... }
```

### Tween Lifecycle Management (CRITICAL)
```csharp
private Tween activeTween;
private Sequence activeSequence;

public void StartAnimation()
{
    // Kill previous tween before starting new one
    activeTween?.Kill();
    activeTween = transform.DOMove(target, duration);
}

private void OnDestroy()
{
    // Always kill tweens on destroy
    activeTween?.Kill();
    activeSequence?.Kill();
    DOTween.Kill(transform);  // Kill all tweens on this transform
    DOTween.Kill(this);       // Kill all tweens using this as ID
}
```

### DOTween Best Practices
| Pattern | Use | Avoid |
|---------|-----|-------|
| Easing | `.SetEase(Ease.OutQuad)` | Linear for all animations |
| Loops | `.SetLoops(2, LoopType.Yoyo)` | Manual loop coroutines |
| Callbacks | `.OnComplete(() => ...)` | Coroutine WaitForSeconds |
| Chaining | Sequences for multi-step | Nested coroutines |
| Cleanup | `DOTween.Kill(target)` | Letting tweens orphan |

## Coroutines (Non-Animation Use Cases)

Use coroutines for: async operations, waiting for conditions, frame-delayed logic.
Use DOTween for: all visual animations, fades, movements, scaling.

```csharp
private Coroutine activeCoroutine;

public void StartProcess()
{
    if (activeCoroutine != null)
        StopCoroutine(activeCoroutine);
    activeCoroutine = StartCoroutine(ProcessRoutine());
}

private void OnDestroy()
{
    if (activeCoroutine != null)
        StopCoroutine(activeCoroutine);
}
```

## Events

| Type | When to Use |
|------|-------------|
| `UnityEvent` | Inspector-configurable, designer-friendly |
| C# `event Action` | Code-only subscriptions |
| `GameEvents` static class | Cross-manager communication |

Always null-check: `OnEvent?.Invoke()`

## ScriptableObjects (with Odin)

```csharp
using Sirenix.OdinInspector;

[CreateAssetMenu(fileName = "NewData", menuName = "Infinity Qube/DataType")]
public class MyData : ScriptableObject
{
    [Title("Configuration")]
    [Required("Value must be set!")]
    [SerializeField] private int value;
    
    [Title("Wave Data")]
    [TableList(ShowIndexLabels = true, DrawScrollView = true)]
    [SerializeField] private List<SpawnEntry> spawns;
    
    [FoldoutGroup("Advanced")]
    [SerializeField] private bool useAdvanced;
    
    [FoldoutGroup("Advanced"), ShowIf("useAdvanced")]
    [SerializeField] private float multiplier = 1f;
    
    [Title("Actions")]
    [Button("Validate Data", ButtonSizes.Large), GUIColor(0.4f, 0.8f, 1f)]
    public void Validate()
    {
        // Validation logic - also callable from inspector
        if (value < 0) value = 0;
    }
    
    private void OnValidate()
    {
        // Auto-validate in editor
        Validate();
    }
}
```

### Odin ScriptableObject Patterns

| Pattern | Use Case |
|---------|----------|
| `[TableList]` | Wave spawns, test commands, any list of structured data |
| `[InlineEditor]` | Nested ScriptableObject references |
| `[Searchable]` | Large lists (attunements, stages) |
| `[Button]` | Expose Validate(), test methods in inspector |
| `[Required]` | Critical fields that must be assigned |

Place instances in `Assets/data/` directory.

## Scene Management

```csharp
// Load scene
SceneManager.LoadScene("SceneName");

// Async load with callback
var operation = SceneManager.LoadSceneAsync("SceneName");
operation.completed += OnSceneLoaded;

// Preserve object across scenes (use sparingly)
DontDestroyOnLoad(gameObject);
```

## Prefab Instantiation

```csharp
// Basic
var instance = Instantiate(prefab, position, rotation);

// With parent
var instance = Instantiate(prefab, parent);

// Cleanup
Destroy(instance);
```
